# * register --chart and svg output

<
2024-01-01
    assets:bank       100
    revenues:salary

2024-01-05
    expenses:food      30
    assets:bank

2024-02-01
    assets:bank       100
    revenues:salary

2024-02-10
    expenses:rent      80
    liabilities:card

# ** 1. Without a report interval, the chart data is the running total after each posting, as a line, by date.
$ hledger -f - reg expenses --chart -O csv
"commodity","series","role","mark","x","value"
"","Total","item","line","2024-01-05","30"
"","Total","item","line","2024-02-10","110"

# ** 2. With a report interval, it is each account's amount in each period, as stacked bars, with the period total as a marker.
$ hledger -f - reg expenses -M --chart -O csv
"commodity","series","role","mark","x","value"
"","expenses:food","item","bar","Jan","30"
"","expenses:food","item","bar","Feb","0"
"","expenses:rent","item","bar","Jan","0"
"","expenses:rent","item","bar","Feb","80"
"","Total","total","marker","Jan","30"
"","Total","total","marker","Feb","80"

# ** 3. A text chart of the running total has a row per posting.
$ hledger -f - reg expenses --chart -w 40
2024-01-05   30  ██████▎
2024-02-10  110  ███████████████████████
